# CHANGELOG

## 0.0.3

* Add support for injection of verilog files into the generated subsystem files

## 0.0.4

* Rename Pulpif to OBI
* Remove interconnects directory, they are in a separate repo
* Add --gen-dot option that enables generation of graphviz dot file, its disabled by default now

## 0.1.6
* Added ~flake.nix~ for reproducible Nix-based development and packaging.

## Unreleased
* Add --tmr option generating the TMR version of a SoC from its non-TMR description: subsystem signals are
  triplicated, interfaces are mapped to their TMR counterpart (tmr_intf property of the interface nodes or
  --intf-map option), and leaf modules are replaced by their TMR definition (<type_name><suffix> or tmr_type
  property). The tmr property set to false excludes a signal or an addrmap instance from triplication.
* The address map package names are based on the non-TMR interfaces, so the non-TMR and TMR SoCs share the
  same package.
* Children with the ispresent property set to false are not generated.
* Fix boolean parameters generated as True/False instead of 1'b1/1'b0.
* Add --intc-pkg option generating the interconnect configuration (number of ports, indexes, and address rules)
  in a separate <top>_intc_pkg package. soc_addr_map_pkg then only contains the memory map, including the
  children not present in the design, so it is shared by all the designs generated from a SystemRDL description.
